# Shell scripts and C headers run or compile on macOS/Linux: always LF, whatever core.autocrlf says
# on the Windows machine that checks them out. A CRLF shebang ("#!/bin/sh\r") fails as "bad
# interpreter" (PRP-11 hit this on a Mac).
*.sh text eol=lf
*.h  text eol=lf

# Files baked into the exes (the application manifest): one byte sequence on every machine, or the stamped exe
# depends on how git checked the file out (PRP-37 found a CRLF checkout changing jr.exe).
*.manifest text eol=lf
